      "About this story": 1,
      "Illustrations are imaginative composites, not portraits or eyewitness scenes. Augustine's life is well recorded, and several scenes here come from his own book, the Confessions, so the story says \"he later wrote.\" The last page is a present-day scene. The story leaves out parts of his early life that are not for children.": 1,
